From f3fb00dcbcb6d19830d14ebe716ab403bc4095ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:13:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/32] (b) v2, part b-3: \caption* label: when to start a
 paragraph and warn

\@caption@nolabel (the label of \caption*) is rewritten as one small
state machine (state P, Q, S or G: something removed or not, in the
group of the label or after its end) with the same removal rules as
before. What changes:

- No false warning when kernel code measures the label: the end of
  \sbox (\color@endgroup) and of \settowidth (\ResumeTagging) and \@
  count as clean (round-2 findings R2V-3, R2-L1).
- A character after the label or after a removed separator ("--", a
  second period) and, directly after the label, a group ({\hskip1zw},
  {}\textsc{:}) now warn; before they were printed silently.
- No warning after the end of a group, as before (class code can
  measure or box the label there); documented, with the remaining
  silent cases (\textit{#1}\textbf{:}, \fbox{#1}:).
- The paragraph is started only when something was removed and \par
  does not follow, in the group of the removed material: a label line
  with a removed period ({\centering #1.\par}) no longer gives an empty
  line.
- Before \\ and \newline the paragraph is always started: #1\\#2 in
  vertical mode no longer gives "There's no line here to end"
  (R2V-4); it gives an empty line and a warning.
- The warning text no longer names \@makecaption (R2-L5).
- The removal layer is documented as separate from the contract (switch
  plus non-empty label), so it can be dropped without changing it.

clsguide, usrguide and changes.txt say "in most cases" warns.

Tests: caption-interface-001 TEST 30 (vertical mode, measuring boxes,
warning cases); .tlg: new warning text and the meaning of the label in
TESTs 21-23 and 27.
